  "summary": "Long-read and multi-tissue RNA-seq resources now map isoform-level regulation to complex traits across lettuce, sheep, and mouse.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is resolving regulatory variation below the gene level and across tissues in non-human species. The lettuce study builds a pan-isoform atlas and ISONET-GWAS framework for isoform-level trait mapping, reporting trans-sQTL hotspots near LsPPR. The mouse atlas profiles age-associated differential transcript usage across brain, liver, and adipose, finding predominantly regulatory isoform switching, with BioEMU modeling used to test structural effects. SheepGTEx provides regulatory variant maps from 6,761 RNA-seq samples across 51 tissues, linked to 34 complex traits. IsoAPA contributes a curated resource of 2.3M transcript-resolved polyadenylation sites from long-read RNA-seq across 816 sample groups. What is new is the shift from gene-level expression to isoform and polyadenylation resolution, which increases the number of testable regulatory units available for association analysis.",
